      "content": "okay, i hear you on the risks. but if we go to the board with \"high risk of rejection,\" they might pull the plug on the whole ANM project, and we've poured months into this. \n\ncan you re-evaluate the landscape if we lean heavily into the co-design aspect? specifically, if we frame the invention not as \"reconfigurable routing\" but as a \"sparsity-driven weight-management system\"? does that change the outlook? i need a sense of whether we can honestly tell the stakeholders that this is a viable, protectable asset that's worth the investment. if we can find a way to steer clear of the 9,876,543 overlap, gives us a cleaner shot, right?",
